<!-- THE WAYPOINT RETICLE. Byte-for-byte iqm_task_open except that it declares NO
     static_border - and it exists ONLY to carry that difference.

     This is the name and the shape the open reticle shipped under until R2.52, brought back
     as a type of its own in R2.55 rather than reverted to. The R2.52 rename was right about
     the SHAPE: a hollow reticle is for any pin that has landed on a mark the map already
     draws, and Personal Adjustable Waypoint was just the first thing that needed one. What
     the rename flattened was that PAW is still special in a way the shape does not capture.

     PAW SUPPLIES ITS OWN ANIMATED RING. Its pin is a real Anomaly task
     (task_placeable_waypoint, storyline = false), and it puts BOTH marks on the same object
     - change_map_location for the task, then map_add_object_spot for its own highlight
     (tasks_placeable_waypoints.script:1547-1548). That highlight is paw_task_default at 39
     units, which modxml_n_iqm_map_icons re-textures to iqm_mapspot_blink. Give this type a
     static_border and a selected waypoint wears TWO concentric pulsing rings on different
     periods, which is worse than the missing one it replaced.

     EVERY OTHER TASK THAT WEARS A HOLLOW RETICLE SUPPLIES NOTHING. A stash mark, a service
     badge, a level changer - none of them animate, so the selection ring is the only moving
     thing on the pin and it has no competition. That asymmetry is the whole reason there are
     two types here instead of one: the trade the old comment described is a good trade
     exactly once, and a bad one everywhere else.

     WHAT DECIDES WHICH. iqm_scan.task_kind returns "waypoint" only from its first branch,
     which tests the task id against task_placeable_waypoint directly, and returns "open"
     from its last, which asks the engine what else is drawn on the target. So this type is
     reachable by exactly one mod's tasks and the split cannot leak.

     Same save rule as every type in this file. -->
<iqm_task_waypoint>
	<level_map spot="iqm_task_waypoint_spot" pointer="quest_pointer"/>
	<mini_map spot="iqm_task_waypoint_spot_mini" pointer="quest_pointer"/>
</iqm_task_waypoint>
<iqm_task_waypoint_spot x="0" y="0" width="19" height="19" stretch="1" alignment="c" location_level="5">
	<texture r="240" g="244" b="248">iqm_mapspot_taskopen</texture>
</iqm_task_waypoint_spot>
<iqm_task_waypoint_spot_mini x="0" y="0" width="19" height="19" stretch="1" alignment="c" location_level="5">
	<texture r="240" g="244" b="248">iqm_mapspot_taskopen</texture>
	<texture_below r="240" g="244" b="248">iqm_mapspot_below</texture_below>
	<texture_above r="240" g="244" b="248">iqm_mapspot_above</texture_above>
</iqm_task_waypoint_spot_mini>
